{"what": "Check of the drawn context buildings against the satellite image, by eye. \"add_osm\": OpenStreetMap building footprints the survey has no building line for (survey m, corner order as in the OpenStreetMap file); \"add_image\": roofs seen in the image where neither the survey nor OpenStreetMap has a building, each a rectangle fitted to the roof by eye, cut back 1 m from every road surface and 0.5 m from every drawn building; \"remove\": outlines (the drawn outline grown 0.75 m) of drawn buildings that stand on open ground in the image: every building line, OpenStreetMap footprint or satellite body lying wholly inside one is not drawn.", "made": "2026-11-13; finished 2026-11-14", "asked": "Aras 13 Nov 2026: 13:06 UTC \"I want you to check every single mm from the satallite photos\"; 13:18 UTC decision card \"Add the buildings the satellite image shows but your survey does not have?\" -> \"Add from OpenStreetMap and satellite\"; 13:20 UTC \"also remove the ones that doesnt exists theere\".", "source": ["Esri World Imagery, Maxar capture of 1 Mar 2023, 0.31 m source, used at 0.5 m in survey coordinates (library/satellite_2026-11-06/sat_2023-03-01_0p5m_survey.jpg), shifted 2 m east and 4 m north onto the survey.", "OpenStreetMap buildings of kit/Data/bergama_osm.osm.", "What the drawing already has: the Basemap cache of 13 Nov 2026 (closed survey building outlines, building lines), the OpenStreetMap footprints in use, kit/Data/houses_sat2023.json."], "method": ["COMPLETE: all 36 pieces read (22 on 13 Nov 2026; the other 14 on 14 Nov 2026: 0250_000, 0500_000, 0500_174, 0500_349, 1250_000, 1250_174, 1500_000, 1750_000, 1750_174, 2500_000, 2500_174, 2750_000, 2750_174, 2750_349, at 5 px per m, removals as boxes in the frame's u, v round the outline): the frame is cut in 36 pieces of 250 m x 180 m at 6 px per m with every drawn outline over the image; 22 of the 36 pieces were read before the work was stopped: 0000_000, 0000_174, 0000_349, 0250_174, 0250_349, 0750_000, 0750_174, 0750_349, 1000_000, 1000_174, 1000_349, 1250_349, 1500_174, 1500_349, 1750_349, 2000_000, 2000_174, 2000_349, 2250_000, 2250_174, 2250_349, 2500_349 (name = west edge u in m, south edge v in m). Only the first 8 removal marks were looked at a second time; the add rectangles were placed and checked by the helper passes only.", "Removed only when most of the outline lies on clearly open ground (bare earth, grass, road, car park) and no roof lies within about 5 m. Hidden under trees, dark roofs, shadow or a dense block where it cannot be told = kept. Heritage buildings are never removed.", "Added from the image only when a roof is clearly seen with both sides 5 m or more and nothing is drawn on it; cars, yards, tarpaulins, containers and greenhouses are not buildings.", "OpenStreetMap footprints: all those the earlier rule left out (no survey building line inside, under 30 % on a closed survey outline), less the ones the image shows as open ground."], "figures": {"add_osm": 227, "add_osm_left_out_open_ground": 1, "add_image": 66, "add_image_m2": 10610, "remove_outlines": 26, "remove_closed_survey": 3, "remove_osm_in_use": 0, "remove_satellite_bodies": 10, "marks_not_used": 2, "unsure_kept_as_drawn": 91, "added_14_nov": {"add_image": 14, "remove": 13}}, "limits": "Read by eye from a 0.5 m image placed to about 5 m: an added rectangle is the roof as seen (eaves, not walls), simplified to a rectangle, and can sit up to about 5 m off. The image is of 1 Mar 2023; anything built or pulled down later is not in it. The south-west corner of the frame has no image and was not checked. Small buildings under trees are not seen. Where it could not be told the drawing was left as it was.", "add_osm": [[[29934.56, 32367.415], [29938.076, 32376.876], [29953.196, 32371.297], [29949.671, 32361.836]], [[30136.08, 31633.018], [30131.368, 31648.738], [30152.59, 31655.042], [30157.293, 31639.322]], [[29583.367, 32648.592], [29588.633, 32650.714], [29590.848, 32645.241], [29585